<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1194">1194</a>–<a href="/years/1250">1250</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Holy Roman Emperor Frederick II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick II was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> and King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in the thirteenth century. Through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jaffa-1229">Treaty of Jaffa</a> in 1229 he obtained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> from the Ayyubid sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil">al-Kamil</a> by negotiation, a concession that al-Kamil made for political support against his Ayyubid rivals.</p></div>
